<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>The <span id="A1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pico-decoder</span> model</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pico-decoder</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Diehl Martinez, 2025</a>)</cite> is a Llama-based <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023</a>)</cite> model, which forms the base of the ablation study investigated in this work. It is illustrated in Figure <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix A The pico-decoder model ‣ Investigating ReLoRA: Effects on the Learning Dynamics of Small Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.12960v1/pico-decoder.svg" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:429/437;" width="429" height="437"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span><span id="A1.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pico-decoder</span>, a Llama-based model</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pico-decoder</span> includes the following features and optimisations:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Root-Mean-Square Layer Normalisation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang and Sennrich, 2019</a>)</cite></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">RoPE embeddings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al., 2023</a>)</cite></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Grouped-query attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ainslie et al., 2023</a>)</cite> with key-value caching</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FlashAttention-2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao, 2023</a>)</cite></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SwiGLU activations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shazeer, 2020</a>)</cite></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Training infrastructure and runtimes</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pico-relora</span> training runs were conducted on a single Ampere GPU node (four GPUs) each, hosted by CSD3. By contrast, the <span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pico-decoder</span> runs were performed on four Ampere nodes (sixteen GPUs).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Ampere nodes are Dell PowerEdge XE8545 servers consisting of two AMD EPYC 7763 64-Core Processors <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.8\text{\,}\mathrm{GHz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.8</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi class="ltx_unit">GHz</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.8\text{\,}\mathrm{GHz}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000\text{\,}\mathrm{GiB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi class="ltx_unit">GiB</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000\text{\,}\mathrm{GiB}</annotation></semantics></math> RAM, four NVIDIA A100-SXM-80GB GPUs, and dual-rail Mellanox HDR200 InfiniBand interconnect. Each A100 GPU is made up of <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6912" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6912</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6912</annotation></semantics></math> FP32 CUDA Cores.<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
            
            
            
          This information is sourced here: <a href="https://docs.hpc.cam.ac.uk/hpc/user-guide/a100.html" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://docs.hpc.cam.ac.uk/hpc/user-guide/a100.html</a>.</span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The wall-clock runtime and total GPU hours of each of the runs are shown in Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix B Training infrastructure and runtimes ‣ Investigating ReLoRA: Effects on the Learning Dynamics of Small Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. For the <span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">tiny</span> models, <span id="A2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pico-relora</span> takes 13.5% fewer GPU hours to train, while for the <span id="A2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">small</span> scale, it was 14.7% more efficient. These are not entirely equivalent comparisons, however, as the <span id="A2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pico-relora</span> runs were configured to checkpoint and evaluate more frequently and with more gradient accumulation steps, alongside other minor differences in the runtime environment.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T3.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="A2.T3.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T3.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wall-clock time</span> / h</th>
<th id="A2.T3.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T3.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPU hours</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T3.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T3.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">t-dec</span></th>
<td id="A2.T3.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A2.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="52.96" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>52.96</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">52.96</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T3.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A2.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="847.37" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>847.37</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">847.37</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T3.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A2.T3.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">s-dec</span></th>
<td id="A2.T3.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A2.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="61.29" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>61.29</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">61.29</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T3.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A2.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="980.56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>980.56</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">980.56</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
