</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Full hyperparameter configurations</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Learning rate scheduler and optimiser configuration – <span id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">shared</span></h3>

<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12960v1/lr-schedulers.png" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/350;" width="476" height="350" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Graph showing the linear LR schedule used by <span id="A3.F8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pico-decoder</span> and ReLoRA’s jagged cosine scheduler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lialin et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. Both are shown here, configured with a total of <math id="A3.F8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30true000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30true000</annotation></semantics></math> steps and an initial warmup of <math id="A3.F8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2000</annotation></semantics></math> steps. The ReLoRA scheduler is additionally configured with <math id="A3.F8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> post-restart warmup steps and a reset frequency of <math id="A3.F8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2000</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ C.1 Learning rate scheduler and optimiser configuration – shared ‣ Appendix C Full hyperparameter configurations ‣ Investigating ReLoRA: Effects on the Learning Dynamics of Small Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> depicts the learning rate and optimisation configurations for both runs. It has an initial linear warmup of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2000</annotation></semantics></math> steps, and resets in line with the ReLoRA frequency specified in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.1 Experimental setup ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Investigating ReLoRA: Effects on the Learning Dynamics of Small Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. After each reset, the learning rate is linearly re-warmed over <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> steps before the standard cosine decay is resumed. The learning rate decays down to a minimum of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math> of the initial rate. The baseline runs use the linear scheduler configured with a <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2500</annotation></semantics></math> step initial warmup. However, as this is indivisible by the <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2000</annotation></semantics></math> step ReLoRA frequency, the jagged cosine scheduler uses the nearest multiple, a <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2000</annotation></semantics></math> step initial warmup. Both schedulers are shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ C.1 Learning rate scheduler and optimiser configuration – shared ‣ Appendix C Full hyperparameter configurations ‣ Investigating ReLoRA: Effects on the Learning Dynamics of Small Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter</span></th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Optimiser</th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T4.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">adamw</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Learning rate</th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="A3.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\text{\times}{10}^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mtext>×</mtext><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\text{\times}{10}^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">LR scheduler</th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><code id="A3.T4.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">relora_jagged_cosine</code></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">LR warmup steps</th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="A3.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2000</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Min LR ratio</th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="A3.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Restart warmup steps</th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="A3.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Learning rate scheduler and optimiser configuration for training runs</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Data configuration – <span id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">shared</span></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ C.2 Data configuration – shared ‣ Appendix C Full hyperparameter configurations ‣ Investigating ReLoRA: Effects on the Learning Dynamics of Small Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> configures the data pipeline for the training runs. The training and perplexity datasets are <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pretokenized-dolma</span> and <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pretokenized-paloma-tinsy</span>, as described in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Training and evaluation datasets: Dolma, Paloma and BLiMP ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Investigating ReLoRA: Effects on the Learning Dynamics of Small Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. The tokeniser used, <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">allenai/OLMo-7B-0724-hf</span>, is the one used for the OLMo model<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
            Which can be found on HuggingFace here: <a href="https://huggingface.co/allenai/OLMo-7B-0724-hf" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/allenai/OLMo-7B-0724-hf</a>.</span></span></span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Groeneveld et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T5" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A3.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter</span></th>
<th id="A3.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T5.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></th></tr>
