<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Model configuration – <span id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">shared</span></h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ C.3 Model configuration – shared ‣ Appendix C Full hyperparameter configurations ‣ Investigating ReLoRA: Effects on the Learning Dynamics of Small Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> depicts the model configuration parameters for the <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">tiny</span> and <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">small</span> training runs. The two runs differ only in their <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>ff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> parameters, keeping the depth of the model and attention architecture constant.</p>
</div>
